 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Eating out in Melbourne cost 3.5% more in August 2026 than in August 2025. That is the ABS \"meals out and take away foods\" category, measured year on year.\n\n- **Recent trend:** The annual rate has stayed between about 3.3% and 4.4% for the past year. It peaked at 4.4% in May 2026 and has eased since, to 3.9% in June, 4.1% in July and 3.5% in August.\n- **Compared with Australia:** The national rate for meals out was 4.1% in August 2026, so Melbourne is rising a bit more slowly than the capital cities as a whole. The national rate was 4.5% in July.\n- **Compared with overall inflation:** Melbourne's all-items CPI rose 3.5% over the year to August 2026, the same as meals out. Nationally, all-items inflation was 4.0%.\n\nFor a year ago, Melbourne's meals-out rate was 3.4% in August 2025. Price rises for eating out have therefore kept running at a similar pace of roughly 3.5% a year.",
